show_help_masscommits() {
  cat <<EOF
my-git masscommits  (aliases: mc, c)

usage: $US [-V|-D] mc [go] [-i|--interactive] [-R|--recursive] [paths...]

Modes (two-phase, same pattern as 'sm'):
  default (no 'go')   ANALYZE — one concise line per repo showing current
                      state and the action 'mc go' WOULD take. No writes,
                      no commits, no pushes. Use this first to audit what
                      would happen.
  go                  APPLY — actually add+commit+push. Commit message is
                      produced automatically (never opens \$EDITOR).

Per-repo output in analyze mode (one line each):
  <path>   CLEAN :))                           -> noop
  <path>   CLEAN (no remote for <branch>)      -> noop
  <path>   CLEAN, ahead=<N>                    -> push
  <path>   DIRTY (N) [M:.. A:.. D:.. ??:..]    -> add+commit+push
  <path>   DIRTY (N) [auto:A user:U]           -> auto-commit A + add+commit[+push]
  <path>   DIRTY (N) [auto:A]                  -> auto-commit A

For each repo in scope (go mode):
  1. Audits .claude setup   (CHECK_CLAUDE_SETUP in config; see: --help claude-check)
  2. If dirty:
       Phase 1 (auto) — bumps + recorded paths are committed TRANSPARENTLY
                        via 'git commit --only', no prompt. See 'Auto-commit
                        of my-git-caused changes' below.
       Phase 2 (user) — anything left is user-dirt: git add -A,
                        auto-generate commit message, git commit -F,
                        and 'git push' ONLY if the repo is in GIT_REPOS.
                        Under -i, this phase prompts [Y]es / [S]kip / [A]bort.
  3. If clean  — checks local-vs-remote; pushes if ahead AND pushable; else DONE

Auto-commit of my-git-caused changes (phase 1):
  my-git must never ASK the user to confirm a change my-git itself made.
  Two categories qualify as my-git-caused:
    (a) Submodule gitlink BUMPS — a path in <repo>/.gitmodules whose
        porcelain entry is 'M'. Super-repo recording a new child SHA is
        housekeeping, not a user decision. Under -R bottom-up walk this
        is the common case: children commit, parent's gitlinks advance.
    (b) PATHS explicitly recorded via _mc_record_change during this mc
        run: .gitignore (when ensure_claude_gitignore appends '.claude/')
        and <repo>/.claude (when ensure_claude_setup migrates a real dir
        to a symlink).
  Both are auto-staged and committed together with subject
      my-git mc: auto-commit (bumps=N recorded=M)
  via 'git commit --only -- <paths>', then pushed if pushable. Nothing
  else is committed in phase 1 — user-dirt stays untouched for phase 2.

Push policy:
  A repo is PUSHABLE iff BOTH conditions hold:
    (1) its absolute path matches an entry in GIT_REPOS (the allowlist), AND
    (2) at least one remote is configured ('git remote' non-empty).
  Everything else (submodules walked via -R, third-party forks, repos
  with no configured remote) gets commit only — no 'git push' attempted.
  In analyze output, non-pushable repos show as '-> add+commit' (no push)
  or 'CLEAN, ahead=N  (<reason> → no push)'.
  Reasons: 'not in GIT_REPOS' | 'no remote configured'.

Scope & recursion:
  default             ONE level — act on the current repo only. A changed
                      submodule HEAD is committed as a gitlink bump, but the
                      submodule itself is NOT entered. This matches git's
                      own model: each super-repo is responsible for its own
                      index, not for what lives inside its submodules.
  -R, --recursive     Walk the full submodule tree BOTTOM-UP. Deepest
                      children commit+push first so each parent's gitlink
                      lands on the freshly-pushed child commit in the same
                      run. Use this when you want ONE command to settle a
                      whole tree of nested repos.

Commit-message template (auto-generated, no editor):
  line 1: intro (filename / short file list / 'AUTOMATIC-MASS-COMMIT')
  body:   #-commented block with file list or diffs + last-N commit messages
          (tunables: COMMIT_MSG_LAST_N, COMMIT_MSG_DIFF_MAX_FILES)

Ignore marker (same signal as 'sm'):
  A nested repo carrying '.git/my-git-submodules.ignore' is treated
  as "leave alone" — mc silently skips it (counted as ignored=N in
  the summary). Use --force to bypass all markers (matches 'sm --force').

Options:
  go                                 Actually commit+push (otherwise: analyze)
  -n, -T, --try, --dry, --dry-run    Synonyms for analyze mode (never acts)
  -i, --interactive                  Per-repo prompt [Y]es / [S]kip / [A]bort
                                      before each commit+push or push-only
                                      action (shows porcelain + commit subject
                                      for commits; divergence log for pushes).
                                      Also governs destructive .claude migration
  -R, --recursive                    Walk the full submodule tree bottom-up
  --force                            Bypass per-repo my-git-submodules.ignore
                                      markers (same as 'sm --force')
  -V, -VV, -D, -DD                   Verbosity / debug
  --help

End-of-run summary:
  mc prints a concise summary (not a full tree) of what was done /
  what's left. For a detailed per-repo status tree, run '$US st'.

Compat:  'my-git go' is a shortcut for 'my-git mc go'.
Scope:   see  $US --help
EOF
}

